@startuml environments_registry
!theme plain
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam groupInheritance 2
skinparam dpi 300

title Environment registry and wrapper

package "deap_pettingzoo.environments" {
    class PettingZooWrapper {
        - env
        + env_name: str
        + env_spec: EnvSpec
        + default_episode_len: int
        + agents: List[str]
        + num_agents: int
        --
        + __init__(env_name, env_config=None, render_mode=None)
        + reset(seed, options) -> observations
        + step(actions) -> tuple
        + observation_space(agent: str) -> Space
        + action_space(agent: str) -> Space
        + render() -> np.ndarray
        + close() -> None
        + {static} supported_envs() -> List[str]
    }
    class EnvSpec <<dataclass>> {
        + name: str
        + factory: Any
        + default_episode_len: int
        + continuous_default: bool
        + notes: str
        + tags: frozenset
        + api: EnvApi
        + wrappers: Tuple[Callable, ...]
        -- api \u2208 {parallel, aec, auto,\n     aec_masked, aec_sequential,\n     jax_parallel} --
    }
    class registry <<module>> {
        + {static} register_env(name, factory, *, api="parallel", wrappers=(), **meta) -> EnvSpec
        + {static} unregister_env(name): None
        + {static} get_env_spec(name) -> EnvSpec
        + {static} is_registered(name) -> bool
        + {static} list_envs(tag=None, api=None) -> List[str]
        + {static} build_env(name, env_config, render_mode)
        + {static} build_env_from_spec(spec: EnvSpec, env_config, render_mode)
        + {static} get_registry_snapshot() -> List[Tuple[str, EnvSpec]]
        + {static} replay_registry_snapshot(snapshot: List[Tuple[str, EnvSpec]]) -> None
        + {static} replay_registry_snapshot_once(snapshot) -> None
        -- build_env_from_spec: no registry lookup;\n   safe for subprocess workers --\n   build_env applies wrappers\n   left-to-right after api coercion --\n   get_registry_snapshot: ProcessPool uses it as\n   initializer/initargs; Dask ships it on the\n   worker spec and calls replay_registry_snapshot_once\n   (idempotent, guarded once-per-process).\n   Non-picklable factory (lambda/closure/local class)\n   -> RuntimeWarning naming the env + dropped;\n   bare module factory (built-ins) dropped silently. --
    }
    class builtin <<module>> {
        auto-registers MPE2 envs\n+ aquarium_v0 (if installed)
    }

note bottom of registry
  EnvSpec.wrappers is an ordered chain
  of plain (env -> env) callables applied
  after api coercion. Typical use is
  composing supersuit transforms
  (pad_observations_v0, pad_action_space_v0,
  agent_indicator_v0, ...).

  get_registry_snapshot() + replay_registry_snapshot()
  propagate custom envs registered in the main
  process into worker subprocesses. The process pool
  passes them as initializer/initargs to make_executor;
  Dask has no initializer hook, so trainers also
  ship the snapshot on each worker spec/payload and the
  worker calls replay_registry_snapshot_once (idempotent,
  guarded once-per-process) before building any env.
  factory must be a picklable callable
  (module-level function / class; not a lambda).

  make_executor resolves the Dask connection as:
  dask_client > scheduler_address arg > DEAP_DASK_SCHEDULER
  env var > auto-built local LocalCluster. A remote target
  (client/address/env var) skips the num_workers<=1 serial
  fast-path and the os.cpu_count() cap — explicit remote
  intent is never silently downgraded or shrunk. On a
  remote cluster, any executor.map worker fn (not just env
  factories) resolving to __main__ raises immediately
  instead of failing opaquely mid-cluster.
end note
}

    PettingZooWrapper ..> registry : resolves env_name
    registry "1" *-- "*" EnvSpec
    builtin ..> registry : register_env

